```tsx
"use client";

export interface WizardPreviewLabels {
  previewTab: string;   // "Aperçu du document"
  formTab: string;      // "Formulaire"
  previewTitle: string;
  locked: string;       // reuse checkout.locked
  pageEstimate: string; // reuse checkout.pages "…page(s) estimée(s)"
  parts: string;       // contract title? use preview.title
}

export function WizardPreviewPanel({ preview, locale, activeKeys, labels }: ...)
```

Actually I planned a shell `WizardWithPreview` that wraps the wizard (children) + panel, holding onStepChange state, plus mobile tabs. Structure:

```tsx
"use client";

function WizardPreviewPanel({ preview, locale, activeKeys }) {
  // Card; scrollable clauses; chunk into pages of up to ~2-3 clauses grouped by character count ~1400 chars/page; footer shows "Page n / N"; 
}

export function WizardWithPreview({ preview, labels, locale, children }) {
  const [activeKeys, setActiveKeys] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [tab, setTab] = useState("form");

  return (
    <div className="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_380px] lg:items-start lg:gap-6">
      <Tabs value={tab} onValueChange={setTab} className="min-w-0">
        {/* mobile tab triggers hidden on lg */}
        <TabsList className="lg:hidden">...</TabsList>
        <TabsContent value="form" className="lg:data-[state=inactive]:block">...
```

Hmm, TabsContent hides inactive by default. On desktop I want both visible. Options: use Tabs only on mobile; simpler: render both children always; on mobile, hide one based on tab state with classNames. That avoids Radix Tabs complexities: use two divs, `className={tab === "form" ? "" : "hidden lg:block"}` etc. With buttons styled as tabs manually (or reuse Tabs with `forceMount`). Simpler manual approach with two Toggle-ish buttons is less code and no a11y downside if I use role="tablist" manually... Simplest accessible: use Tabs from ui/tabs with forceMount on both contents and CSS hiding.

Actually simplest robust: plain state + aria:

```tsx
<div className="flex gap-1 lg:hidden" role="tablist" aria-label={labels.previewAria}>
  <button role="tab" aria-selected={tab==='form'} ...>{labels.formTab}</button>
  <button role="tab" aria-selected={tab==='preview'} ...>{labels.previewTab}</button>
</div>
<div className={cn("min-w-0", tab === "form" ? "" : "hidden lg:block")} role="tabpanel">{children}</div>
<div className={cn("min-w-0", tab === "preview" ? "" : "hidden lg:block")} role="tabpanel">...panel</div>
```

That is clean. Preview panel content:

