Several issues:
1. `makeRule` spread order: `...overrides` first but `code`/`title` assigned before → spread at end overrides defaults properly. Error at line 23 "'code' is specified more than once" — my object has `code: overrides.code` then `...overrides` — TS complains. Restructure: put `...overrides` spread FIRST then explicit defaults for other fields? Cleaner: destructure:

```ts
const { code, route, title, ...rest } = overrides;
return {
  id: ...,
  code,
  title: title ?? code,
  ...defaults,
  route,
  ...rest,
};
```

Simpler: build base with code/route required, spread rest:

```ts
function makeRule(params: Partial<RoutingRuleDefinition> & { code: string; route: RoutingRoute }) {
  const { code, route, ...rest } = params;
  return {
    id: `rule_${++id}`,
    code,
    title: rest.title ?? code,
    ...defaults,
    route,
    ...rest,
  };
}
```

But route still duplicated (route in defaults is required type — defaults omit route; include route after defaults). Wait `defaults` must have route (RoutingRuleDefinition requires route). Provide `route` in the final object after defaults — defaults can't include route since not known yet... just spread defaults then route then rest (rest may include route=undefined? no — destructured out). OK.

2. Five test failures — SELF_SERVICE cases fail. Why? Tests expecting SELF_SERVICE: standard lease with rentAmountMad 5000; freelance without ip; NDA durationYears 2; vehicle salePrice 65000; and the unverified LEGAL_REQUIREMENT masking case. The ones passing: LAWYER_OPTIONAL, LAWYER_REQUIRED cases, real estate, commercial, pending, empty, jurisdiction.

Hypothesis: rules with failing conditions produce `notMatched` entries; decideRoute: matched.length === 0 → `selection.notMatched.length > 0` → undetermined. For lease standard + rent 5000: single rule with no conditions should match → SELF_SERVICE... but it FAILED. So matched is empty even without conditions?! Wait — maybe `evaluateConditions(rule.conditions, input.caseData)` with empty conditions works. Hmm.

Or... `matched.length === 0` and `selection.excluded.some(...)` false, `notMatched` — what's in notMatched? A rule tested but not matched. With one rule matched there is no notMatched. But the test failed — what did decide return? I don't know the actual value. Possibility: the router scans `route-merge`/`router-parts` createAssembler: the assemble() of merged requires contractType? Maybe "assemble" sets status/route... Let me debug: run a single quick vitest to print the actual route. Actually easier to look at route-merge + assemble briefly.

